\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1 Ten thousand times ten thousand, 
\par In sparkling raiment bright, 
\par The armies of the ransomed sints 
\par Throng up the steps of light;
\par Tis finished, all is finished,
\par Their fight wih death and sin;
\par Filing open wide the golden gates, 
\par And let the victors in.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2 What rush of hallelujahs 
\par Fills all the earth and sky!
\par What ringing of a thousand harps 
\par Bespeaks the triumph nigh!
\par O day for which creation 
\par And all its tribes were made!
\par O joy, for all its former woes 
\par A thousand-fold repaid!
\par 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3 O then what raptured greetings 
\par On Canaans happy shore, 
\par What knitting severd friendships up
\par Where partings are no more! 
\par Then eyes with joy shall sparkle 
\par That brimmed with tears of late;
\par Orphans no longer fatherless, 
\par Nor widow desolate.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4 Bring near Thy great salvation, 
\par Thou Lamb for sinners slain;
\par Fill up the roll of Thine elect,
\par Then take Thy power and rign;
\par Appear, Desire of nations-
\par Thine eixiles long for home;
\par Show in the heaven Thy promised sign;
\par Thou Prince and Savioru, come. 
\par Amen.
\par 
\par 
